From ced211b8a8e65f1f437dc1b836de2054bbce55ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:01:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(conftest): HERMES_TEST_REQUIRE_EXTRAS fails a listed
 extra's importorskip instead of skipping [daveey]

#762 (6e0d15a0e7) guarded 139 test files with module-level pytest.importorskip for aiohttp.test_utils,
acp and keyring so a minimal venv collects. In a CI lane that installs those extras, the same guard
would silently skip the files if an extra were dropped from the install, with CI green.

- tests/_fixtures/required_extras.py: when HERMES_TEST_REQUIRE_EXTRAS lists top-level module names,
  tests/conftest.py wraps pytest.importorskip at import time: a listed module is imported directly and
  a missing one raises ImportError naming it and the variable (collection error). Unlisted modules keep
  the skip; unset leaves pytest.importorskip untouched.
- scripts/run_tests.sh: forward HERMES_TEST_REQUIRE_EXTRAS through the env -i allowlist.
- tests.yml: set HERMES_TEST_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=keyring,aiohttp,acp in the test slices and the upgrade
  e2e lane, the two lanes that install --extra all + keychain.
- tests/test_conftest_required_extras.py: listed+missing raises, unlisted+missing skips, unset skips,
  plus end-to-end collection through the real conftest for all three.

Card t_01a1a1058c3145b3.
